{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_35","type":"agent_message","text":"Early results favor seasonality: all completed crypto comparisons improved, generally by about **1–2% CRPS**, and gold’s first window improved by **5.24%**. Recent-volatility adaptation alone has produced smaller gains. Next I’ll test whether heavier tails and uncertainty about future volatility help, particularly for the one-hour score’s volatility component."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_36","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 2 — innovation tails and volatility uncertainty\n\nHypothesis: a Gaussian with a point volatility forecast understates both return tails and uncertainty in realized volatility. Compare Student-t innovations (df=5, unit variance) and lognormal path-level volatility uncertainty (log std=0.35, unit second moment), each added separately to seasonal EWMA.\n\nChange: two 1000-path suites on the same pre-registered windows and prompts. Keep fast/slow volatility and seasonal profiles identical.\n\nKill criterion: require improvement across both windows and most asset cells; do not retain a distribution merely because its field position improves.\n\nResult / Verdict: pending. Diagnostics of calendar effects are recorded separately; no calendar changes in these experiments.\nEOF\nuv run agent/run_suite.py --tag mixture --model research_model --workers 2 --config '{\\\"seasonal\\\":true,\\\"mix\\\":0.35}' > agent/results/mixture_suite.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_19","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > /tmp/update_predict.py <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\np=Path('agent/predict.py');s=p.read_text();start=s.index('    for t in times:\\\\n',s.index('def generate('));end=s.index('    return len(times)',start)\ns=s[:start]+'''    from itertools import groupby\n    from time import perf_counter\n    begin = perf_counter()\n    for day, day_times in groupby(times, key=lambda t: t.date().isoformat()):\n        day_times = list(day_times)\n        runs = []\n        for t in day_times:\n            context = prices.loc[t - pd.Timedelta(minutes=CONTEXT_MINUTES):context_end(t, time_length)]\n            out = simulate(asset=asset, start_time=t.isoformat(), time_increment=time_increment,\n                           time_length=time_length, num_simulations=num_simulations, context_prices=context)\n            runs.append(np.asarray(out[2:], dtype=np.float64))\n        root = out_dir / asset / f\\\"{time_length}_{time_increment}\\\"\n        root.mkdir(parents=True, exist_ok=True)\n        np.save(root / f\\\"date={day}.npy\\\", np.stack(runs))\n        (root / f\\\"date={day}.json\\\").write_text(json.dumps({\n            \\\"start_times\\\": [t.isoformat() for t in day_times], \\\"asset\\\": asset,\n            \\\"time_increment\\\": time_increment, \\\"time_length\\\": time_length,\n            \\\"num_simulations\\\": num_simulations, \\\"num_steps\\\": time_length // time_increment + 1}))\n    print(f\\\"generation seconds/prompt: {(perf_counter()-begin)/len(times):.4f}\\\", flush=True)\n''' +s[end:]\ns=s.replace('    ap.add_argument(\\\"--asset\\\", default=\\\"BTC\\\")','    ap.add_argument(\\\"--asset\\\", default=\\\"BTC\\\")\\\\n    ap.add_argument(\\\"--model\\\", default=\\\"modeling\\\", help=\\\"agent module providing simulate\\\")')\ns=s.replace('    args = ap.parse_args()','    args = ap.parse_args()\\\\n    import importlib\\\\n    global simulate\\\\n    simulate = importlib.import_module(args.model).simulate')\np.write_text(s)\nPY\nuv run python /tmp/update_predict.py\ncat > agent/run_suite.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Bounded parallel official-backtester experiments, with durable per-cell artifacts.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport argparse, subprocess, os\nfrom concurrent.futures import ThreadPoolExecutor\nfrom pathlib import Path\n\nCRYPTO = ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']\nCOM = ['XAU','NVDAX','GOOGLX','TSLAX','AAPLX','WTIOIL','SPCX','SP500']\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('--tag',required=True);p.add_argument('--model',default='modeling');p.add_argument('--ends',nargs='+',default=['2026-09-16','2026-10-10']);p.add_argument('--days',type=int,default=2);p.add_argument('--workers',type=int,default=4);p.add_argument('--assets',nargs='+',default=CRYPTO+COM);p.add_argument('--formats',nargs='+',default=['24h','1h']);p.add_argument('--paths',type=int,default=1000)\na=p.parse_args();root=Path('agent/results')/a.tag;root.mkdir(parents=True,exist_ok=True)\ndef run(cell):\n asset,fmt,end=cell;prefix=root/f'{asset}_{fmt}_{end}'\n if prefix.with_suffix('.json').exists():return\n cmd=['uv','run','agent/predict.py','--asset',asset,'--model',a.model,'--days',str(a.days),'--eval-end',end,'--num-simulations',str(a.paths),'--latest-formula','--output',str(prefix)]\n if fmt=='1h':cmd+=['--time-length','3600','--time-increment','60']\n env=dict(os.environ,OPENBLAS_NUM_THREADS='1',OMP_NUM_THREADS='1',MKL_NUM_THREADS='1')\n with prefix.with_suffix('.log').open('w') as f:r=subprocess.run(cmd,stdout=f,stderr=subprocess.STDOUT,env=env)\n print(prefix,r.returncode,flush=True)\n if r.returncode:raise RuntimeError(str(prefix))\ncells=[(asset,fmt,end) for end in a.ends for asset in a.assets for fmt in a.formats if fmt=='24h' or asset in CRYPTO]\nwith ThreadPoolExecutor(max_workers=a.workers) as pool:list(pool.map(run,cells))\nPY\nuv run agent/run_suite.py --tag baseline --model baseline > agent/results/baseline_suite.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
