{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_41","type":"agent_message","text":"Seasonality improved all 18 asset/format comparisons in the September window, including an average **7.52% reduction for commodities/equities**. Tail-model results are mixed so far, so neither is selected yet. Calendar diagnostics also show distinct announcement spikes and sharply lower activity during exchange holidays; I’ll test those on separate event and weekend windows."}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_42","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > agent/fit_events.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Pooled event multipliers, with event dates as independent sampling units.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport json\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport numpy as np,pandas as pd\nx=pd.read_csv('agent/results/event_diagnostics.csv')\nx['group']=np.where(x.asset.isin(['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE']),'crypto','other')\nx['ratio']=x.ratio.clip(.02,100)\nout={}; diagnostics=[]\nfor (group,event,lo),g in x.groupby(['group','event','lo']):\n if event in ['EARNINGS','NYSE_CLOSED','NYSE_EARLY_CLOSE'] or lo==120:continue\n # Assets at one release share a shock: collapse to one datum per release.\n z=g.groupby('time').ratio.median()\n if len(z)<4:continue\n estimate=float(np.exp(.67*np.log(z).median()))\n estimate=max(1.,min(12.,estimate))\n loeo=[float(np.exp(.67*np.log(z.drop(i)).median())) for i in z.index]\n diagnostics.append(dict(group=group,event=event,lo=int(lo),n_dates=len(z),mult=estimate,leave_one_out_min=min(loeo),leave_one_out_max=max(loeo)))\n out.setdefault(group,{}).setdefault(event,{})[str(lo)]=estimate\nPath('agent/event_multipliers.json').write_text(json.dumps({'train_end_exclusive':'2026-09-01','groups':out},indent=2))\npd.DataFrame(diagnostics).to_csv('agent/results/event_fit.csv',index=False)\nprint(pd.DataFrame(diagnostics).round(3).to_string(index=False))\nPY\nuv run agent/fit_events.py\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
