{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_46","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '280,355p' .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/synth/validator/crps_calculation.py && tail -5 agent/results/seasonal_suite.log && tail -4 agent/results/scale85_suite.log\"","aggregated_output":"\n    Parameters:\n        price_paths (numpy.ndarray): Array of simulated price paths.\n        interval_steps (int): Number of steps that make up the interval.\n        absolute_price (bool): If True, absolute price values (rather than price changes) are returned.\n\n    Returns:\n        numpy.ndarray: Array of price changes over intervals.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Get the prices at the interval points\n    # [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] -> [1, 3, 5, 7] if interval_steps is 2\n    interval_prices = price_paths[:, ::interval_steps]\n    if is_gap:\n        # [1, 2, 3, 4, 5, 6, 7] -> [1, 3] if interval_steps is 2\n        interval_prices = interval_prices[:, :2]\n\n    # Calculate price changes over intervals\n    if absolute_price:\n        return interval_prices[:, 1:]\n\n    return (\n        np.diff(interval_prices, axis=1) / interval_prices[:, :-1]\n    ) * 10_000\n\n\ndef block_volatilities(\n    price_paths: np.ndarray, block_steps: int\n) -> np.ndarray:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculate the volatility of each consecutive block of a price path.\n\n    Parameters:\n        price_paths (numpy.ndarray): Array of price paths.\n        block_steps (int): Number of steps that make up a block.\n\n    Returns:\n        numpy.ndarray: Standard deviation, in basis points, of the step\n        returns inside each block. A block with fewer than two observed\n        returns is NaN so that it can be skipped; the steps left over after\n        the last whole block are dropped.\n    \"\"\"\n    returns = (np.diff(price_paths, axis=1) / price_paths[:, :-1]) * 10_000\n\n    n_blocks = returns.shape[1] // block_steps\n    blocks = returns[:, : n_blocks * block_steps].reshape(\n        returns.shape[0], n_blocks, block_steps\n    )\n\n    # Only the scorable blocks go through nanstd: it warns on a block with\n    # fewer than two observed returns, which is the tolerated case here.\n    scorable = np.sum(~np.isnan(blocks), axis=2) >= 2\n    volatilities: np.ndarray = np.full(scorable.shape, np.nan)\n    volatilities[scorable] = np.nanstd(blocks[scorable], axis=1, ddof=1)\n\n    return volatilities\nagent/results/seasonal/AAPLX_24h_2026-10-10 0\nagent/results/seasonal/GOOGLX_24h_2026-10-10 0\nagent/results/seasonal/WTIOIL_24h_2026-10-10 0\nagent/results/seasonal/SPCX_24h_2026-10-10 0\nagent/results/seasonal/SP500_24h_2026-10-10 0\nagent/results/scale85/SOL_24h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/scale85/ETH_1h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/scale85/XRP_24h_2026-09-16 0\nagent/results/scale85/SOL_1h_2026-09-16 0\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_47","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat agent/BUDGET.md && cat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 4 — genuinely prospective calendar information\n\nHypothesis: event times improve forecasts beyond an EWMA because they are known before the return shock. Pool normalized event variance by asset group but collapse assets to one observation per event date. Fit through August only. Use 2/3 shrinkage in log multiplier and no suppression for nonsignificant macro bins. Shared GDP/PCE announcements combine by maximum, never multiplication. Calendar is loaded from SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR inside simulate; missing file/types are tolerated.\n\nLOEO diagnostic: crypto CPI first-five-minute multiplier 3.46 (leave-one-event-out 2.80–4.28); FOMC 3.83 (2.89–4.15), next25m 2.35 (1.81–3.11). The units are conditional variance multipliers, not CRPS gains. Leave-one-event-out here checks fit stability; final test is entirely later event dates. Raw diagnostics retained in results/event_fit.csv.\n\nChange: enable future event variance only, plus an explicit 0.15 variance factor during calendar NYSE closures for concerned equities. Exact overlap integrates each event kernel over predicted steps. Compare seasonal model without events versus with events on three NEW three-day windows ending Sep09 (holiday/weekend), Sep19 (FOMC), Oct05 (NFP/weekend). These are stress validation windows, not claimed to be untouched after selection.\n\nKill criterion: require paired CRPS improvement on event-affected prompts across more than one release/window. Reject if any overall configuration regresses materially (>0.2%) without clear support. Holiday and macro effects will be separated if necessary.\n\nResult / Verdict: pending.\nEOF\nuv run agent/run_suite.py --tag stress_seasonal --model research_model --days 3 --ends 2026-09-09 2026-09-19 2026-10-05 --workers 4 --config '{\\\"seasonal\\\":true}' > agent/results/stress_seasonal_suite.log 2>&1\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
