{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_50","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"sed -n '95,123p' .venv/lib/python3.12/site-packages/synth_lib/benchmark/generate_predictions.py && du -sh agent/results && git status --short\"","aggregated_output":"\n\ndef load_simulate(modeling_path: Path) -> Callable:\n    spec = importlib.util.spec_from_file_location(f\"candidate_{modeling_path.parent.name}\", modeling_path)\n    assert spec is not None and spec.loader is not None  # always true for a .py file path\n    module = importlib.util.module_from_spec(spec)\n    spec.loader.exec_module(module)\n    return module.simulate\n\n\ndef store_root(data_root: Path, asset: str) -> Path:\n    root = data_root / STORE_SUBDIR / asset / \"1m\"\n    if not root.exists():\n        raise FileNotFoundError(f\"no minute store for {asset}: {root} does not exist\")\n    return root\n\n\ndef load_minute_prices(data_root: Path, asset: str, start: pd.Timestamp, end: pd.Timestamp) -> pd.DataFrame:\n    \"\"\"Minute OHLCV over [start, end] from daily partitions. Missing partitions raise: a silent\n    hole here would shrink every context that spans it without anyone noticing.\"\"\"\n    root = store_root(data_root, asset)\n    frames = []\n    day = start.date()\n    while day <= end.date():\n        path = root / f\"date={day.isoformat()}.parquet\"\n        if not path.exists():\n            raise FileNotFoundError(f\"missing partition {path}\")\n        try:\n            frames.append(pd.read_parquet(path, columns=[\"timestamp\", *OHLCV_COLUMNS]))\n4.1M\tagent/results\n M agent/journal.md\n M agent/run_suite.py\n?? agent/BUDGET.md\n?? agent/analyze_events.py\n?? agent/event_multipliers.json\n?? agent/fit_events.py\n?? agent/research_model.py\n?? agent/results/\n?? agent/seasonality.json\n?? agent/summarize.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_51","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"uv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\ns=Path('agent/research_model.py').read_text()\ns=s.replace(\\\"config=json.loads(os.environ.get('MODEL_CONFIG','{}'))\\\", \\\"config={'seasonal': True}\\\")\nPath('agent/modeling.py').write_text(s)\nPY\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\nIteration 1 completed: seasonality wins all 36 matched asset/format/window cells. Official mean CRPS (equal asset averages within configuration): September baseline→seasonal crypto24h 4313.4987→4244.4702; com/equ24h 2342.5058→2156.2219; crypto1h 1115.1929→1094.7930. October: crypto24h 4285.8943→4240.6629; com/equ24h 2229.7086→2111.5626; crypto1h 911.4830→891.1912. 1000 paths throughout. Verdict: KEEP seasonal EWMA as provisional serving model; no nomination while further experiments remain worthwhile. Flat EWMA alone: discard for 24h; October all five crypto24h cells regressed, and com/equ mean also regressed. Lesson: deterministic future time-of-week information is more useful here than merely shortening volatility memory.\nEOF\ncat > agent/suggestions.md <<'EOF'\n# Suggestions for the benchmark and future work\n\n- The campaign says BUDGET.md is at the workspace root; this run's harness writes agent/BUDGET.md. Align the documented location.\n- Keep the raw-context issuance cutoff explicit. The supplied evaluator originally took the last 10080 rows before issuance; the official generator uses the seven calendar days ending at issuance. This run aligns with the official generator.\n- Daily NumPy predictions substantially reduce serialization overhead compared with one JSON file per prompt. The official loader already supports them; make this the default in the starter evaluator.\n- Calendar data sometimes co-locates GDP and PCE. Treat their effects jointly instead of estimating independent additive effects from the same release observations.\nEOF\nuv run python - <<'PY'\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport os,time,numpy as np,pandas as pd\nfrom synth_lib.benchmark.generate_predictions import load_simulate,load_minute_prices,context_end\nfn=load_simulate(Path('agent/modeling.py'));t=pd.Timestamp('2026-10-10',tz='UTC')\nfor asset,h,s in [('BTC',3600,60),('BTC',86400,300),('AAPLX',86400,300)]:\n frame=load_minute_prices(Path('market_data'),asset,t-pd.Timedelta(days=7),t).loc[:context_end(t,h)]\n os.environ['SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED']='99';start=time.perf_counter();out=fn(asset,str(t),s,h,1000,frame);elapsed=time.perf_counter()-start\n a=np.asarray(out[2:]);assert a.shape==(1000,h//s+1) and np.isfinite(a).all() and (a[:,0]==frame.close.dropna().iloc[-1]).all()\n b=np.asarray(fn(asset,str(t),s,h,7,frame)[2:]);assert b.shape[0]==7\n assert np.array_equal(b,np.asarray(fn(asset,str(t),s,h,7,frame)[2:]))\n os.environ['SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED']='100';assert not np.array_equal(b,np.asarray(fn(asset,str(t),s,h,7,frame)[2:]))\n print(asset,h,'latency',round(elapsed,4),'nan-close',int(frame.close.isna().sum()))\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
