{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_67","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/bash -lc \"cat > agent/report.md <<'EOF'\n# Calendar-time volatility for Synth price-path simulation\n\nResearch in progress. No final champion has been nominated.\n\n## Context\n\nSynth scores an ensemble of price paths using CRPS: the forecast must express uncertainty at several return horizons, not merely predict the terminal price. The one-hour configuration also scores realized volatility. This campaign uses only the frozen minute-price snapshot through October 11, 2026, and the provided calendar. All reported CRPS comes from the pinned official backtester, at the validator's 1000-path ensemble size and actual prompt times. Earlier one-hour prompts are rescored with the latest volatility-inclusive formula.\n\n## Approach\n\nThe first useful addition is predictable calendar-time variation. Fit weekday/weekend half-hour variance profiles in New York time on June–August prices, before the validation windows. Normalize by a rolling volatility level, combine squared and absolute-return estimates, and shrink the profiles toward a common level. Estimate current volatility from the seven-day context after removing that recurring shape; combine fast and slow exponentially weighted estimates and gradually revert forecasts toward the slower estimate. Restore the known future seasonal shape along each simulated path.\n\nUse one-minute returns for one-hour forecasts and five-minute returns for 24-hour forecasts. NaN observations remain missing: no interpolation, no fabricated prices, and no treating a multi-minute gap as a one-minute return. The seed is read from SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED. Path count and length honor the caller's arguments.\n\n## Experiments\n\nThe seeded starter is a constant-volatility lognormal random walk. Shortening volatility memory alone yields small, inconsistent improvements for 24-hour paths. The seasonal model improves all 36 asset/format/window cells in two initial validation windows: two scored days ending September 16 and two ending October 10.\n\nTests of a global 15% width reduction, Student-t innovations, and path-level lognormal volatility uncertainty are underway. The width reduction already fails to improve the crypto 24-hour forecasts consistently. Heavy tails have smaller, horizon-dependent effects than seasonality.\n\nA separate calendar study uses event dates as independent observations, pooling assets within each release before measuring uncertainty. Announcements at the same minute, such as GDP and PCE, are not counted twice. Prospective event tests use later CPI/PPI, FOMC, and payroll windows. A planned holiday test was abandoned because the available scored-prompt bundle begins on September 8; the official backtester cannot aggregate a one-prompt window. This failed run is documented, not counted as a model result.\n\n## Results\n\nThese are official mean CRPS values, averaged equally across assets within each configuration. They are provisional validation results, not the unseen ten-day campaign score.\n\n| Scored window end | Configuration | Starter | Seasonal EWMA |\n|---|---|---:|---:|\n| 2026-09-16 | CRYPTO_24H | 4313.499 | 4244.470 |\n| 2026-09-16 | COM_EQU_24H | 2342.506 | 2156.222 |\n| 2026-09-16 | CRYPTO_1H | 1115.193 | 1094.793 |\n| 2026-10-10 | CRYPTO_24H | 4285.894 | 4240.663 |\n| 2026-10-10 | COM_EQU_24H | 2229.709 | 2111.563 |\n| 2026-10-10 | CRYPTO_1H | 911.483 | 891.191 |\n\nOn the available CPU, the provisional model generated 1000 paths in 0.017 seconds for BTC one-hour and 0.041 seconds for a 24-hour forecast. The sparse AAPLX context tested had 3495 missing close observations and produced valid paths. Small arbitrary ensemble counts and repeatable/changeable seeds also passed contract checks.\n\n## Limitations\n\nThe initial evaluation covers four scored days, so the apparent consistency is encouraging but not a full regime test. Adjacent 24-hour prompts overlap substantially; prompt count is not independent sample size. Seasonal profiles may drift as these young perpetual markets mature. Cached validator paths and minute candles differ in missingness and stale prices. Event types have few independent dates, and some release effects cannot be separated. No rank improvement is used as evidence of model improvement.\n\n## What more budget is for\n\nBroader weekend/event validation, finer weekly and within-hour seasonality, volatility-mixture calibration, and independent-seed checks. These studies are ongoing; final selection will be based on paired CRPS and reproducibility rather than a favorable field rank.\nEOF\ncat >> agent/journal.md <<'EOF'\n\n## Iteration 5 — finer recurring clock structure (prepared)\n\nHypothesis: the weekday/weekend profile misses day-specific transitions and within-hour clustering. Fit a seven-day profile shrunk 50% to the two-group profile, and separately fit minute-of-hour variance profiles for crypto. Training stays June–August.\n\nMeasurement: shrunk first-minute variance factors are 1.18–1.29, minute30 factors 1.22–1.41; first-five-minute/rest ratios 1.12–1.19. These are variance diagnostics only. Learned artifacts: seasonality_weekly.json and clock.json. Both optional extensions are implemented in research_model but NOT selected in modeling.py.\n\nNext: test each separately at 1000 paths on the initial matched windows, then stress windows if consistent. Kill criterion: require improvements across both initial windows and most assets in the affected configuration; do not stack unvalidated adjustments.\nEOF\ncat > agent/paired.py <<'PY'\n\\\"\\\"\\\"Display paired daily official CRPS differences; no metric reimplementation.\\\"\\\"\\\"\nimport argparse\nfrom pathlib import Path\nimport pandas as pd\np=argparse.ArgumentParser();p.add_argument('candidate');p.add_argument('baseline');a=p.parse_args();rows=[]\nfor f in (Path('agent/results')/a.candidate).glob('*.parquet'):\n b=Path('agent/results')/a.baseline/f.name\n if not b.exists():continue\n x=pd.read_parquet(f);y=pd.read_parquet(b)\n keys=['asset','time_length','start_time','scored_time']\n d=x[keys+['crps']].merge(y[keys+['crps']],on=keys,suffixes=('_new','_base'))\n d=d[(d.crps_new>0)&(d.crps_base>0)]\n d['day']=pd.to_datetime(d.scored_time).dt.strftime('%Y-%m-%d');rows.append(d)\nif not rows:raise SystemExit('No paired results yet.')\nx=pd.concat(rows).drop_duplicates(['asset','time_length','start_time','scored_time'])\nx['config']=x.apply(lambda r:'CRYPTO_1H' if r.time_length==3600 else 'CRYPTO_24H' if r.asset in ['BTC','ETH','SOL','XRP','HYPE'] else 'COM_EQU_24H',axis=1)\ng=x.groupby(['config','asset','day'])[['crps_new','crps_base']].mean();g['change']=g.crps_new/g.crps_base-1\nprint(g.groupby(['config','day']).change.agg(['mean','min','max','count']).mul({'mean':100,'min':100,'max':100,'count':1}).round(4).to_string())\nPY\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
